# short-description: Single partition rootfs with UUID and no bootloader
# long-description: Creates a partitioned image with a single partition in
# use and does not contain a bootloader.
#
# ${S4SK_WIC_EXT4_OPTS} is expanded by bitbake (do_write_wks_template) from
# conf/machine/rcars4.inc, so mkfs flags are machine-configurable metadata
# rather than hardcoded in the wks. wic's own default is "-F -i 8192".
# -b 4096: ext4 block size must match the UFS logical block size (4096);
# U-Boot ext4load and the kernel cannot read a 1024-byte-block ext4 from a
# 4096-sector device (superblock at fs offset 1024 is not sector-aligned).
part / --source rootfs --use-uuid --fstype=ext4 --label root --align 4096 --mkfs-extraopts "${S4SK_WIC_EXT4_OPTS}"
